  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Philippines: Sustainable Training and Education in the Philippines for Justice Professionals &#x2013; Part B</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To ensure that justice sector trainers in Metro Manila and the regions meet the needs of the institutions they support. 2) To ensure that the Supreme Court (SC), the Department of Justice (DOJ), the Office of the Ombudsman (OMB) and the Anti-Money Laundering Council (AMLC) have capacity development agencies that are well-managed and sustainable. 3) To ensure that the SC, the DOJ, the OMB and the AMLC collaborate to innovate professional capacity development.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: the Supreme Court, the Department of Justice, the Office of the Ombudsman, the Anti-Money Laundering Council, justice sector professionals, particularly trainers, judges and prosecutors.Indirect beneficiaries: Wider population of the Philippines.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to develop the professional capacity of Philippine justice sector institutions to continuously improve the knowledge and skills of their staff and thereby improve the quality of justice delivery for the public.</narrative>
  </description>
